{"name":"Golden Scarab","hex":"#eddb8e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"scarab","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A beetle of the species Scarabaeus sacer, sacred to the ancient Egyptians.","Any species of beetle belonging to the family Scarabaeidae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scarab"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scarab (artifact)","blocks":[{"text":"Scarabs are amulets and impression seals shaped according to the eponymous beetles, which were widely popular throughout ancient Egypt. They survive in large numbers today, and through their inscriptions and typology, these artifacts prove to be an important source of information for archaeologists and historians of ancient Egypt, representing a significant body of its art."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Scarab_of_Sithathoryunet_with_the_Name_of_Amenemhat_III_MET_16.1.22_bot.jpeg/330px-Scarab_of_Sithathoryunet_with_the_Name_of_Amenemhat_III_MET_16.1.22_bot.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarab_(artifact)","wikidata":"Q2442735"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c